cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Expanse, please cite it using the metadata in this file. Once the project has a Zenodo record, cite its concept DOI (all versions) or the version DOI of the release you used."
title: "Expanse: clean-room, pure-Rust Judy arrays with a drop-in libjudy-compatible C ABI"
type: software
abstract: "Expanse is a clean-room, pure-Rust implementation of Judy arrays — sparse, dynamic associative structures built as 256-ary digital tries partitioned by key range (expanse) rather than by population — modernized for current 64-bit and 32-bit embedded microarchitectures. It ships libexpanse, a high-performance drop-in C ABI replacement for libjudy, plus Go, Node.js, .NET and Python bindings."
authors:
  - family-names: "Brousse"
    given-names: "Nicolas"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7649-1668"
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/orieg/expanse"
url: "https://github.com/orieg/expanse"
keywords:
  - judy-array
  - radix-tree
  - trie
  - data-structures
  - rust
  - libjudy
  - associative-array
